    "body": "RADIO temporal grouping constructs scalar-tensor `max_seqlen_q` and `max_seqlen_kv` values even though `PackedSeqParams` declares integer maxima. With FlashAttention 4.0.0b34 and CUTLASS 4.8, these values fail in `cute.ceil_div` with `ValueError: Expected IntTuple, whose leaves are integers`.\n\nKeep the maximum as the Python integer already computed from frame geometry. This preserves cumulative sequence boundaries and their dtype/device, and avoids the unnecessary scalar allocation without adding a device-to-host synchronization.\n\nThe issue affects five image/video tests in [Megatron Bridge #6258](https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Megatron-Bridge/pull/6258), including [the two RADIO video forwards](https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Megatron-Bridge/actions/runs/37924987528/job/113823958424). Add six CPU regression cases covering uniform videos, ragged videos, mixed images/odd-frame videos, and both embedder paths; also enforce integer maxima in the existing GPU metadata cases.\n\nValidation:\n\n- 12 targeted CPU tests passed in the 26.09 container. The six new cases all fail against the original implementation at the integer-type assertion.\n- The repository formatter check passed for both changed files (Black, isort, Pylint, Ruff); whitespace checks passed. Mypy encountered an internal tool error, so type checking is not claimed as passed.\n- All six existing CUDA metadata cases passed on RTX 6000 Ada with the fixed commit, covering host/CPU/CUDA geometry and both duplication modes. Cumulative boundaries retain their CUDA device and dtype, and maximum lengths are Python integers. This is metadata validation, not full-model or FA4 kernel coverage.\n- The [upstream RADIO/models job](https://github.com/NVIDIA/Megatron-LM/actions/runs/37937170763/job/113855736895) passed all 52 RADIO cases, including all six new regressions and six strengthened metadata cases; none was skipped. This run checked out merge `41d49831` (fix `38a2399` into upstream main `204867ba`) with PyTorch 26.08, rather than the raw fork commit or Bridge's 26.09 runtime.\n- [Upstream CI](https://github.com/NVIDIA/Megatron-LM/actions/runs/37937170763) completed successfully: all 42 unit jobs and all ten default functional jobs passed. Required CODEOWNER review remains pending; this CI result does not satisfy the human review gates.\n- [Current Bridge CI](https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Megatron-Bridge/actions/runs/37948803805), on head `d9500bb6c` / merge `e8f2b7b4` with MCore `38a2399` and PyTorch 26.09, passed 11,737 core tests and 573 diffusion tests. Both image builds, lint, and import validation passed. All six affected GPU targets explicitly passed: the packed optimizer step (92.78 s), packed image, multiframe video, ragged rectangular video, exact rectangular image/video token counts, and vision data parallelism. None was skipped; the pin-consistency check also passed.\n- All five local Bridge pin checks passed. Bridge functional tests and separate installation/release acceptance remain pending as of 2026-10-09 15:47 UTC. No attention backend, numerical tolerance, or test selection is changed by this MCore patch.\n\nThe branch starts at `441a987409b8fdd2b90b463f7999bac970109a43`, the MCore revision used by the reproducing Bridge CI run. RADIO and its test file are unchanged between that revision and current main.\n",
